  "id": "flaky-network-test",
  "title": "Sandbox integration test times out on a docs-only PR",
  "description": "A PR to example-org/fx-rates only edits README.md and docs/setup.md, yet the test job fails in 'Integration tests (sandbox)': 'fetches latest rates from sandbox' hits the client's 5000ms AbortSignal timeout against sandbox.rates.example.com while the other four sandbox tests and every unit test pass. Nothing in the diff can affect runtime behaviour, and the job history on main shows the same job failing on 2 of the last 10 runs on unrelated commits. The right call is flaky (an external sandbox timing out), recommend a rerun, and optionally harden the test (retry on timeout, longer timeout, or stub the sandbox). 'infrastructure' is accepted because the proximate cause is a network timeout to a third-party host; 'code' is wrong.",
