  "changedFiles": [
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "status": "modified",
      "additions": 5,
      "deletions": 1,
      "patch": "@@ -10,6 +10,10 @@\n convert(100, \"GBP\", \"USD\", table);\n ```\n \n+`convert` rounds half-to-even to the target currency's minor units (0 for JPY, 3 for KWD).\n+\n ## Development\n \n-See [docs/setup.md](docs/setup.md).\n+Node 24 (see `.nvmrc`). Unit tests run offline; integration tests call the sandbox and are\n+skipped unless `RATES_SANDBOX_URL` and `RATES_SANDBOX_API_KEY` are set.\n+See [docs/setup.md](docs/setup.md) for the full guide.",
      "previousPath": null
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/setup.md",
      "status": "modified",
      "additions": 25,
      "deletions": 1,
      "patch": "@@ -1,6 +1,30 @@\n # Local setup\n \n+## Prerequisites\n+\n+- Node 24 (`nvm use` reads `.nvmrc`)\n+- A sandbox API key from the rates developer portal (optional, only for integration tests)\n+\n+## Install and test\n+\n ```bash\n npm ci\n-npm test\n+npm run test:unit                 # offline, with coverage\n ```\n+\n+## Integration tests\n+\n+The integration project talks to the hosted sandbox. Export the URL and your key first:\n+\n+```bash\n+export RATES_SANDBOX_URL=https://sandbox.rates.example.com\n+export RATES_SANDBOX_API_KEY=<your sandbox key>\n+npm run test:integration\n+```\n+\n+Without both variables the integration suites are skipped.\n+\n+## Releasing\n+\n+Bump the version in `package.json`, merge to `main`, then tag `vX.Y.Z`; the release workflow\n+publishes to the internal registry.",
      "previousPath": null
    }
